Purchase Rate

Validate that Purchase Rate is populated correctly in the NCMI output from APR Percentage Applied Amount and review the populated volume and value range for unexpected values.


Purchase Rate should be populated from APR Percentage Applied Amount where the source value is available.

Populated Purchase Rate values should be numeric and no unexpected values should be present.



SELECT
    COUNT(*) AS RECORD_COUNT,

    SUM(COALESCE(APPLICATION_COUNT, 0)) AS APPLICATION_VOLUME,

    COUNT_IF(PURCHASE_RATE IS NOT NULL) AS PURCHASE_RATE_POPULATED,

    COUNT_IF(PURCHASE_RATE IS NULL) AS PURCHASE_RATE_NULL,

    MIN(PURCHASE_RATE) AS MIN_PURCHASE_RATE,

    MAX(PURCHASE_RATE) AS MAX_PURCHASE_RATE,

    CASE
        WHEN COUNT_IF(PURCHASE_RATE IS NOT NULL) > 0
        THEN 'PASS'
        ELSE 'FAIL'
    END AS TEST_RESULT

FROM BDP_UK_CARDS.FACT_CARD_AGGREGATOR_APPLICATION_SUMMARY;